SHELL(1)

NAME
    shell - start the SmallOS command shell

SYNOPSIS
    shell [--line-mode]
    shell -c command

DESCRIPTION
    shell starts the interactive SmallOS command shell. It is normally launched
    at boot after the kernel mounts ext2.

    The shell resolves external commands from /bin, /usr/bin, and /usr/sbin.
    Native SmallOS commands remain preferred. If a bare command is not found,
    the shell tries /usr/bin/busybox with the command name as a BusyBox applet.
    A command containing a slash is treated as a path.

    The shell also implements a small set of built-ins for navigation,
    background jobs, and tests. External programs can be launched by typing
    their command name directly.

OPTIONS
    --line-mode
        Use simple line input instead of the interactive input path.

    -c command
        Execute one command line and exit.

BUILT-INS
    help
        Show the command summary.

    cd path
        Change the shell working directory.

    pwd
    wd
        Print the shell working directory.

    bg path [arg ...]
        Execute a program as a reattachable background job.

    jobs
        List reattachable background jobs.

    fg jobid
        Reattach and wait for a background job.

    kill jobid
        Terminate a background job.

    selftest
        Run installed userland self-tests.

    shelltest
        Run built-in shell parser and dispatch tests.

    clear
        Clear the terminal.

    exit
        Exit the shell.

PIPES
    A simple pipeline operator is supported:

        command1 | command2 | command3

SEE ALSO
    busybox(1), sh(1), cd(1), jobs(1), fg(1), bg(1)
